are\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nEmergency Pet Care When Your Pet’s Life is on the Line\nServing more than 15,000 patients a year, the MedVet Diley Hill team is a trusted partner in care for family veterinarians and pet lovers on the Southeast side of Columbus in Fairfield and Franklin counties and the surrounding areas.\nWe serve as an extension of your family veterinarian by providing advanced, comprehensive veterinary emergency care. You’ll find caregivers with the expertise and state-of-the-art resources to diagnose and treat your beloved pet during critical times. We know your pet is an important part of your family, and emergencies can be stressful, so we treat your pet like our own and communicate with you each step of the way as we work to deliver the best outcome for your pet.\nIf your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our hospital – no appointment is needed.\nMedVet Diley Hill Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nEmergency Medicine\nOur Hospital Leaders\nEllen Neal, DVM\nMedical Director\nPaula Miller\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nLara Dickey\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nTiffany Elgersma\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nLindsey Elster\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKirk Forte\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKaitlin Gutherman\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nLisa Harrison\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJessica Hemmelgarn\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nCrystal King\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAlec Land\n, DVM, MS\nEmergency Medicine\nZoe I. Marinacci\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMolly Miller\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nEllen Neal\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKyle Relyea\n, DVM\nAllison Schroeder\n, DVM, MS\nEmergency Medicine\nJacqueline K. Shook\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMaddy Vesoulis\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nShow All Doctors (\n16\n)\nPet Stories\n“\nOur Miniature Pinscher, Murphy, was hospitalized for pancreatitis and received absolutely the best care. The incredibly helpful, compassionate staff made me feel completely at ease. They ensured I understood his condition, treatment plan, and home care. They called the next day to check on him. Can’t recommend this emergency vet more.”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
